  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.4.7\n            Fixed:\n            - Fixed TypeConverter type parameter order: all built-in converters now correctly use TypeConverter<TProvider, TModel> (provider type first, model type second).\n            - Fixed EnumToIntConverter, EnumToStringConverter, DynamicEnumToStringConverter, GuidToStringConverter, ListToJsonConverter type definitions.\n            - Fixed Source Generator using FromProvider instead of ToProvider when binding parameters for Insert/Update operations.\n            - Fixed ConverterGenerator Setter method incorrectly calling ToProvider when assigning already-converted model values.\n            - Fixed DaoCacheGenerator using wrong conversion direction for database parameter binding.\n            - Added numeric type conversion in TypeConverterInvoker to handle type mismatches across all providers (SQLite Int64, SQL Server Int32/Int64, PostgreSQL, MySQL).\n            - Added legacy data compatibility: string values in database are automatically parsed to numeric types for backward compatibility with older versions.\n            - Renamed BoolConverter to BoolToIntConverter and ByteConverter to IntToByteConverter for naming consistency.\n            - Updated all documentation examples to reflect correct TypeConverter usage.\n            \n            0.4.6 (hotfix)\n            Fixed:\n            - Fixed a codegen bug where DAO Insert methods returning int did not return the execution result in the generated DaoImpl.\n            - Improved return-type handling for Insert to support numeric return types (e.g., int, long, and other numeric primitives), ensuring the generated implementation correctly returns the value.\n            \n            0.4.5\n            - Added strict compile-time SQL verification for [Query] (Room-style):\n                - Error on unknown tables referenced in FROM/JOIN.\n                - Error on unknown columns referenced anywhere in the query (SELECT list, WHERE/ON/SET, ORDER BY/GROUP BY when applicable).\n                - Error on missing SQL parameters (e.g., @id/:id without a matching method parameter).\n                - Error on parameter type mismatch when compared/assigned to an entity column (e.g., long column vs string parameter).\n                - Error on SELECT result type mismatch vs the queried table/entity (e.g., SELECT * FROM documents returning List<Note>).\n            - Tooling implemented with incremental, method-scoped analysis to avoid performance regressions.\n            \n            0.4.4\n            - Fluent Migration DX: Column chaining, convenience methods (Id, Timestamps, SoftDelete), and TypeAffinity alias.\n            - Programmatic Seeding API: db.SeedAsync() for MAUI/mobile apps, SeederOptions, SeederContext builder pattern.\n            - RoomSeeder<TDatabase>: Strongly-typed base class for cleaner seeder implementations.\n            - Security: Fixed SQL injection in SchemaGenerator.TableExists() using parameterized queries.\n            - Stability: Fixed potential deadlock in ObservableQuery.Publish() with DeliveryMode.All.\n            - Fixed compiler warnings CS8509 and CS8601.\n            - Updated CLI make:seeder template with new helper methods.",
